                          P e r s o n a l   C 6 4
                        ---------------------------
                        The C64 emulator for the PC
                        ---------------------------

Run PC64.EXE and press F1 for online help. The contents page has a quick
start info.


                            More documentation
                            ------------------

ORDER.DOC      Cable infos, distributor addresses and order form.

GAMES.DOC      Optimal settings for some games. All programs in GAMES.DOC
               work with PC64. If a game doesn't run, it has been treated
               with a non compatible packer.


                            System requirements
                            -------------------

- IBM AT with 486DX2-66 CPU. Personal C64 runs also on a 386SX-25, but not
  with original speed.

- A VGA graphic card. Only mode 13h is used which should work with every
  card. Speed is very important as old VGA cards can add up to 130(!) wait
  states to each video RAM access. New cards reduce this to 10 wait states
  in ISA bus. VL and PCI bus will be even faster.

- DOS since version 3.3 or the DOS emulations in Windows 3.1, OS/2 2.1,
  Windows NT 3.5 and Linux 1.1.64 to 1.1.73 with dosemu 0.53.35. NT doesn't
  allow sound, transfer between the PC and the C64 or external joysticks.

- At least 480 Kb low RAM. The more you have free, the faster is the
  desktop.

- A hard disk with about 4 Mb free. You can reduce this to 1.3 Mb by
  deleting the bundled games.

The following hardware isn't necessary but will be supported:

- For the desktop a Microsoft compliant mouse and appropriate driver.

- An AdLib compliant sound card for SID voices 1 to 3 and a Soundblaster
  compliant DSP for digitized samples over the volume register. The dialog
  box <Options / Sound> shows which sound hardware has been detected.

- A PC gameport card and an analog or digital IBM joystick (registered
  version only).

- A digital C64 joystick and the Alternate joystick adapter on LPTx
  (registered version only).

- For transferring files the PC64 cable and a C64 or C128 with any drive
  on IEC bus or expansion port, not on userport (registered version only).

- A CD ROM drive. This is in provision for third party vendors who want to
  bring out a CD with C64 games.


                       Limits of the shareware version
                       -------------------------------

- The transfer between the PC and the C64 is disabled. For testing purposes,
  <Manager / Clone L64> and <Options / Waitstates> are working.

- External joysticks are disabled, i.e. IBM analog on a game card and C64
  digital on the Alternate joystick adaptor. You must use the white arrows
  on the numeric pad and the right control key.

- A shareware message will be displayed and must be confirmed when you leave
  PC64.

- No printed manual, PC64 cable and Alternate joystick adapter.

To get the registered version without these limitations, please fill out the
form in ORDER.DOC and send it to your local distributor.


                                  Updates
                                  -------

The license information for the full version is located in the file
LICENSE.DAT. As all versions since 1.03 work with the same licensing file,
the emulator can be updated from the shareware evaluation versions. Simply
install the new shareware version on the old licensed version, and you will
get a new licensed version. This applies for all PC64 versions with major
version number 1, e.g. version number 1.x.

You can get the newest shareware version can be obtained from your
acquaintances, or from BBS systems, like:

* CompuServe, Magna Forum, Library 4, PC64*.ZIP

* ftp.funet.fi:/pub/cbm/emulation/pc64/pc64*.zip

* frodo.hiof.no:/pub/c64/emulator/pc64*.zip

* watson.mbb.sfu.ca:/pub/c64/emulator/pc64*.zip

The version 2.0 should be ready in autumn 1995, and it will run completely
under Windows. Licensed users will be informed, as the new version comes
available. The update will cost about 15-20 American dollars.


