                            License conditions:
                            -------------------

You may install Personal C64 on all your computers. You may also copy the
program for friends and acquaintances and upload it to BBSes, as long as the
licensing file is not included. Never give the file LICENSE.DAT to anyone!
It contains your name and the serial number in encrypted form, so that the
author can easily find out the origin of any illegal copies.


                                Disclaimer:
                                -----------

Before connecting the PC and the C64, you must switch off all related
equipment, also the TV set or monitor on the C64! All equipment must be
connected to the same wall outlet, to avoid current loops. The user port
connector may not be connected the wrong way around in any case, or the PC's
printer port will get broken! Broken TV sets may lead high voltage to the
antenna connector, killing the CIA chip when you connect the C64 with the
grounded PC.

The manufacturer is not responsible for any defects in the interfaces that
are caused by not following these rules!


                          Who owns the system ROMs?
                          -------------------------

The C64 ROMs are copyrighted by Commodore, BASIC V2 is copyrighted by
Microsoft. I've written a letter to the German sites of both companies on
07-27-97 and asked them for the permission to distribute the system ROMs
together with Personal C64. On 08-02-94, Commodore has directed me to the
mother company in the USA.

Because there was no reaction since then, I've decided to distribute the
ROMs without the explicit permission. If Commodore or Microsoft will forbid
that, you'd have to connect the C64 or the C128 with the PC64 cable and run
the command <Manager / Read ROMs>.
